F315                             ; their handlers, at ejmp.)
F315                             ; =============================================================================
F315                             ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
F315                             ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
F315                             ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
F315                             ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
F315                             ;  short calls. Prints
F315                             ; 
F315                             ;     CR LF
F315                             ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
F315                             ;     Stk n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
F315                             ;     Rtn n CR LF
F315                             ; 
F315                             ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
F315                             ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
F315                             ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
F315                             ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
F315                             ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
F315                             ; 
F315                             ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 80FEh): the
F315                             ;  report's own cells then reach 8 bytes further down, to 80F6h, into the
F315                             ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
F315                             ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
F315                             ; =============================================================================
F315   10 CE 80 F0  ERROR:    LDS   #RSREP   
F319   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
F31B   8D 34                  BSR   pmsg   
F31D   0D 0A 45 72 72 A0      FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
F323   1F 98                  TFR   B,A   
F325   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F328   8D 27                  BSR   pmsg   
F32A   20 40 A0               FCB   " @"," "+80h   
F32D                             ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
F32D                             ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
F32D   10 8E 00 00            LDY   #0   
F331   8E 82 7F               LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
F334   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F336   8E 82 FF               LDX   #PROG-1   
F339   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F33B   24 23                  BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
F33D   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F33F   31 21        LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
F341   30 01        LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
F343   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F345   24 19                  BHS   lc3   
F347   A6 84                  LDA   ,X   
F349   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F34B   26 F4                  BNE   lc2   
F34D   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F34F   20 EE                  BRA   lc1   
F351                             ; pmsg: print the text after the call, up to and including the character
F351                             ; that has bit 7 set (it is printed without it), then return after it.
F351                             ; (It sits here, in the middle of the report, where all its calls reach.)
F351   35 10        PMSG:     PULS   X   
F353   A6 84        PM1:      LDA   ,X   
F355   84 7F                  ANDA   #7Fh   
F357   BD F3 E8               JSR   putc   
F35A   6D 80                  TST   ,X+   
F35C   2A F5                  BPL   pm1   
F35E   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F360   DC 36        LC3:      LDD   <AT   
F362   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F364   ED C4                  STD   ,U   ; the column
F366   36 20                  PSHU   Y   
F368   BD F3 D0               JSR   pdec   ; the line
F36B   8D E4                  BSR   pmsg   
F36D   AC                     FCB   ","+80h   
F36E   8D 60                  BSR   pdec   ; the column
F370   8D DF                  BSR   pmsg   
F372   0D 0A 53 74 6B A0      FCB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
F378                             ; the data stack: its depth, then its top 8 cells, from Y down to
F378                             ; the program's top cell, at ,U.
F378   34 40                  PSHS   U   ; where the walk ends
F37A   CC 81 FC               LDD   #DSTOP   
F37D   A3 E4                  SUBD   ,S   
F37F   8D 3F                  BSR   pdh   ; the depth (pdec leaves U as it was)
F381   8D CE                  BSR   pmsg   
F383   BA                     FCB   ":"+80h   
F384   31 C8 10               LEAY   16,U   ; past the 8th cell from the top ...
F387   10 8C 81 FC            CMPY   #DSTOP   
F38B   24 08                  BHS   sl1   
F38D   8D C2                  BSR   pmsg   ; (there are more than 8)
F38F   20 2E 2E AE            FCB   " ..","."+80h   
F393   20 04                  BRA   sl2   
F395   10 8E 81 FC  SL1:      LDY   #DSTOP   ; ... or the whole stack, if no more than 8
F399   10 AC E4     SL2:      CMPY   ,S   
F39C   23 0B                  BLS   sl9   
F39E   EC A3                  LDD   ,--Y   
F3A0   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F3A2   8D AD                  BSR   pmsg   
F3A4   A0                     FCB   " "+80h   
F3A5   8D 1F                  BSR   h_num   
F3A7   20 F0                  BRA   sl2   
F3A9   8D A6        SL9:      BSR   pmsg   
F3AB   0D 0A 52 74 6E A0      FCB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
F3B1   CC 81 00               LDD   #RSTOP   ; the return stack's depth, (RSTOP - S) / 2,
F3B4   93 3A                  SUBD   <SSAV   ;   S as it was when this character began
F3B6   8D 08                  BSR   pdh   
F3B8   BD F3 51               JSR   pmsg   
F3BB   0D 8A                  FCB   13,10+80h   
F3BD   7E FF 09               JMP   EXIT   
F3C0                             ; pdh: print D/2 (a depth: D is twice it), unsigned.
F3C0   44           PDH:      LSRA      
F3C1   56                     RORB      
F3C2   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F3C4   20 0A                  BRA   pdec   
F3C6                          ENDIF      
F3C6                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
F3C6   6D C4        H_NUM:    TST   ,U   
F3C8   2A 06                  BPL   pdec   
F3CA   86 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
F3CC   8D 1A                  BSR   putc   
F3CE   8D 5E                  BSR   negt   
F3D0                             ; pdec: print the top cell as unsigned and drop it, by recursion on /10
F3D0   CC 00 0A     PDEC:     LDD   #10   
F3D3   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F3D5   8D 68                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = quotient, TOS = digit
F3D7   37 06                  PULU   D   ; the digit
F3D9   34 04                  PSHS   B   
F3DB   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F3DD   27 03                  BEQ   pd1   
F3DF   8D EF                  BSR   pdec   ; (it drops the quotient)
F3E1   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAU)
F3E2   33 42        PD1:      LEAU   2,U   ; drop the zero quotient
F3E4   35 02                  PULS   A   
F3E6   8B 30                  ADDA   #"0"   ; and fall into putc
F3E8   7E FF 03     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   
F3EB                             ; ---- more arithmetic ---------------------------------------------------------
F3EB   EC C1        H_AND:    LDD   ,U++   
F3ED   A4 C4                  ANDA   ,U   
F3EF   E4 41                  ANDB   1,U   
F3F1   20 04                  BRA   st   
F3F3   EC C1        H_ADD:    LDD   ,U++   
F3F5   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F3F7   ED C4        ST:       STD   ,U   
F3F9   39                     RTS      
F3FA                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
F3FA   BD F0 BB     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
F3FD   25 2C                  BLO   negnum   
F3FF   EC 42                  LDD   2,U   
F401   A3 C1                  SUBD   ,U++   
F403   20 F2                  BRA   st   
F405                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F405                             ; "/" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F405                             ; second range: the divide itself and the routines after it.
F405                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F405                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F405                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
F405                             ; it stops with Z, both operands still on the stack.
F405                H_DIV:       
F405                          IF   CHECKED   
F405   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F407   10 27 FF 05            LBEQ   e_zero   
F40B                          ENDIF      
F40B   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F40D   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a's sign: for r
F40F   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F411   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a xor b: for q
F413   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F415   8D 22                  BSR   absx   ; |a|
F417   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F419   8D 1E                  BSR   absx   ; |b|
F41B   8D 22                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = q, TOS = r
F41D   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F41F   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F421   2A 02                  BPL   dv1   
F423   8D 0B                  BSR   negx   ; q's sign
F425   6D E0        DV1:      TST   ,S+   
F427   2A 0F                  BPL   ng9   
F429   20 03                  BRA   negt   ; r's sign
F42B   BD F0 C2     NEGNUM:   JSR   rdnum   ; a negative literal: read it, then negate
F42E   1F 31        NEGT:     TFR   U,X   
F430   EC 84        NEGX:     LDD   ,X   ; negx: negate the cell at X
F432   40                     NEGA      
F433   50                     NEGB      
F434   82 00                  SBCA   #0   
F436   ED 84                  STD   ,X   
F438   39           NG9:      RTS      
F439   6D 84        ABSX:     TST   ,X   ; absx: negate the cell at X if negative
F43B   2A FB                  BPL   ng9   
F43D   20 F1                  BRA   negx   
F43F                             ; udiv: unsigned divide, in place. The dividend is the NOS cell and the
F43F                             ; divisor the TOS cell, both <= 8000h; the NOS cell becomes the quotient and
F43F                             ; the TOS cell the remainder. The remainder is built in D (always < the
F43F                             ; divisor, so 2R+1 fits in 16 bits).
F43F                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
F43F   EC C4        UDIV:     LDD   ,U   
F441   83 00 02               SUBD   #2   
F444   26 07                  BNE   ud0   
F446   64 42                  LSR   2,U   
F448   66 43                  ROR   3,U   ; the quotient
F44A   59                     ROLB      ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D was 0)
F44B   20 18                  BRA   ud3   
F44D   8E 00 10     UD0:      LDX   #16   
F450   4F                     CLRA      
F451   5F                     CLRB      
F452   68 43        UD1:      ASL   3,U   
F454   69 42                  ROL   2,U   ; the dividend's top bit ...
F456   59                     ROLB      
F457   49                     ROLA      ; ... into the remainder
F458   10 A3 C4               CMPD   ,U   
F45B   25 04                  BLO   ud2   
F45D   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F45F   6C 43                  INC   3,U   ; a quotient bit
F461   30 1F        UD2:      LEAX   -1,X   
F463   26 ED                  BNE   ud1   
F465   ED C4        UD3:      STD   ,U   
F467   39                     RTS      
F468                             ; =============================================================================
F468                             ;  The grave's codes (h_grave is the dispatcher). Each is entered with
F468                             ;  A = the character, and ends in RTS.
F468                             ; 
F468                             ;    `!  ( addr -- )        call the machine code at addr. The code is
F468                             ;                           entered with the address already popped: U
F468                             ;                           points at the top data cell (big-endian) and the
F468                             ;                           dispatcher's return address is on top of S. It
F468                             ;                           may pop and push data cells by changing U; on
F468                             ;                           return the cell at ,U is the new TOS. It must
F468                             ;                           keep Y, DP and S (balanced) and return with RTS;
F468                             ;                           A, B, X and CC may change.
F468                             ;    `$  ( addr -- addr' )  the hex loader: pairs of hex digits are stored
F468                             ;                           from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS
F468                             ;                           (39h) is written and its address is left. An odd
F468                             ;                           last digit is consumed and dropped.
F468                             ;    `'  ( -- )             new line: CR LF
F468                             ;    `+  ( addr -- n )      add 1 to the cell at addr and leave its new value
F468                             ;    `,  ( n -- r )         a random number from 0 to n-1 (n is 1 to 32767)
F468                             ;    `-  ( addr -- n )      subtract 1 from the cell at addr, the same way
F468                             ;    `.  ( -- addr )        the address of the random seed
F468                             ;    `<  ( a b -- n )       the smaller of the two (signed)
F468                             ;    `>  ( a b -- n )       the larger
F468                             ;    `?  ( flag -- )        the cursor off (0) or on
F468                             ;    `@  ( row col -- )     the cursor to that row and column, both from 0
F468                             ;    `^  ( -- )             clear the screen and home the cursor
F468                             ;    `_  ( -- )             clear from the cursor to the end of the line
F468                             ; 
F468                             ;  Neither the loader's stores nor the machine code are checked.
F468                             ; =============================================================================
F468                             ; The table: a character, then its handler's distance from the address
F468                             ; after that byte.
F468   21           GTAB:     FCB   "!"   
F469   B0                     FCB   g_exec-$-1   
F46A   24                     FCB   "$"   
F46B   80                     FCB   g_hex-$-1   
F46C   27                     FCB   27h   
F46D   76                     FCB   g_nl-$-1   
F46E   2B                     FCB   "+"   
F46F   3E                     FCB   g_inc-$-1   
F470   2C                     FCB   ","   
F471   11                     FCB   g_rnd-$-1   
F472   2D                     FCB   "-"   
F473   3A                     FCB   g_inc-$-1   
F474   2E                     FCB   "."   
F475   55                     FCB   g_seed-$-1   
F476   3C                     FCB   "<"   
F477   5F                     FCB   g_min-$-1   
F478   3E                     FCB   ">"   
F479   57                     FCB   g_max-$-1   
F47A   3F                     FCB   "?"   
F47B   B1                     FCB   g_cur-$-1   
F47C   40                     FCB   "@"   
F47D   D1                     FCB   g_at-$-1   
F47E   5E                     FCB   "^"   
F47F   9C                     FCB   g_cls-$-1   
F480   5F                     FCB   "_"   
F481   A3                     FCB   g_eol-$-1   
F482                          IF   CHECKED   
F482   00                     FCB   0   ; the end
F483                          ENDIF      
F483                             ; `, The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes every 16-bit
F483                             ; value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones and the low
F483                             ; ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low (EOR) before the
F483                             ; remainder of dividing by n is taken.
F483                             ; n must be 1 to 32767: the checked build stops with Z on anything less
F483                             ; than 1.
F483                G_RND:       
F483                          IF   CHECKED   
F483   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F485   83 00 01               SUBD   #1   ; n - 1 negative: n is 0 or less
F488   10 2B FE 84            LBMI   e_zero   
F48C                          ENDIF      
F48C   D6 76                  LDB   <SEED   ; (the cell is little-endian)
F48E   96 77                  LDA   <SEED+1   
F490   58                     ASLB      
F491   49                     ROLA      
F492   58                     ASLB      
F493   49                     ROLA      
F494   1A 01                  ORCC   #1   ; (the carry is the + 1)
F496   D9 76                  ADCB   <SEED   
F498   99 77                  ADCA   <SEED+1   ; * 5 + 1
F49A   9B 76                  ADDA   <SEED   ; + * 256: * 261 + 1
F49C   D7 76                  STB   <SEED   
F49E   97 77                  STA   <SEED+1   
F4A0   D8 77                  EORB   <SEED+1   
F4A2   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F4A4   BD F2 BE               JSR   h_swap   ; the dividend under n
F4A7   8D 96                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = the quotient, TOS = the remainder
F4A9   37 06                  PULU   D   
F4AB   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F4AD   39                     RTS      
F4AE                             ; `+ and `-: one routine. "," minus the character is 1 or -1.
F4AE   AE C4        G_INC:    LDX   ,U   
F4B0                          IF   CHECKED   
F4B0   BD F3 02               JSR   chkst   ; both bytes are tested first, as "!" does
F4B3   30 01                  LEAX   1,X   
F4B5   BD F3 02               JSR   chkst   
F4B8   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F4BA                          ENDIF      
F4BA   40                     NEGA      
F4BB   8B 2C                  ADDA   #","   
F4BD   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   
F4BF   1D                     SEX      
F4C0   EB 84                  ADDB   ,X   ; (the cell is little-endian)
F4C2   A9 01                  ADCA   1,X   
F4C4   E7 84                  STB   ,X   
F4C6   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F4C8   ED C4                  STD   ,U   ; the new value is TOS
F4CA   39                     RTS      
F4CB                             ; `. pushes the address of the random seed.
F4CB   8E 82 76     G_SEED:   LDX   #LET+SEED   
F4CE   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F4D0   39                     RTS      
F4D1                             ; `< and `>: b is taken off and compared with a; it goes in a's place if it
F4D1                             ; is the one wanted.
F4D1   8D 0B        G_MAX:    BSR   gcmp   
F4D3   2F 08                  BLE   gm9   
F4D5   20 04                  BRA   gm8   
F4D7   8D 05        G_MIN:    BSR   gcmp   
F4D9   2C 02                  BGE   gm9   
F4DB   ED C4        GM8:      STD   ,U   
F4DD   39           GM9:      RTS      
F4DE   EC C1        GCMP:     LDD   ,U++   
F4E0   10 A3 C4               CMPD   ,U   ; b - a
F4E3   39                     RTS      
F4E4   86 0D        G_NL:     LDA   #13   
F4E6   8D 64                  BSR   gputc   
F4E8   86 0A                  LDA   #10   
F4EA   20 60                  BRA   gputc   
F4EC   AE C4        G_HEX:    LDX   ,U   
F4EE   8D 18        HX1:      BSR   hexc   
F4F0   24 0F                  BCC   hx2   
F4F2   C6 10                  LDB   #16   
F4F4   3D                     MUL      ; B = the digit, moved up to the high half
F4F5   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; (an odd digit is overwritten by the RTS)
F4F7   8D 0F                  BSR   hexc   
F4F9   24 06                  BCC   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
F4FB   AA 84                  ORA   ,X   
F4FD   A7 80                  STA   ,X+   
F4FF   20 ED                  BRA   hx1   
F501   86 39        HX2:      LDA   #39h   ; RTS
F503   A7 84                  STA   ,X   
F505   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F507   39                     RTS      
F508                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
F508                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
F508                             ; return with the carry clear.
F508   BD F0 BB     HEXC:     JSR   isdig   
F50B   25 0A                  BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
F50D   84 DF                  ANDA   #0DFh   
F50F   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   
F511   81 06                  CMPA   #6   
F513   24 04                  BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
F515   80 F6                  SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
F517   31 21        HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
F519   39           HV9:      RTS      
F51A   37 80        G_EXEC:   PULU   PC   ; jump to it: the code's RTS returns to the
F51C                             ;   dispatcher
F51C                          IF   ANSI   
F51C                             ; `^: ESC [ H homes the cursor, and ESC [ J clears from there to the end of
F51C                             ; the screen. `_: ESC [ K clears to the end of the line. (CONOUT keeps B.)
F51C   8D 28        G_CLS:    BSR   csi   
F51E   86 48                  LDA   #"H"   
F520   8D 2A                  BSR   gputc   
F522   C6 4A                  LDB   #"J"   
F524   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDB)
F525   C6 4B        G_EOL:    LDB   #"K"   
F527   8D 1D                  BSR   csi   
F529   1F 98                  TFR   B,A   
F52B   20 1F                  BRA   gputc   
F52D                             ; `? ( flag -- ): ESC [ ? 2 5 l hides the cursor, ESC [ ? 2 5 h shows it.
F52D   8D 17        G_CUR:    BSR   csi   
F52F   86 3F                  LDA   #"?"   
F531   8D 19                  BSR   gputc   
F533   86 32                  LDA   #"2"   
F535   8D 15                  BSR   gputc   
F537   86 35                  LDA   #"5"   
F539   8D 11                  BSR   gputc   
F53B   AE C1                  LDX   ,U++   ; the flag
F53D   27 03                  BEQ   gc1   
F53F   86 68                  LDA   #"h"   
F541   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDA)
F542   86 6C        GC1:      LDA   #"l"   
F544   20 06                  BRA   gputc   
F546                             ; csi: print ESC [, which starts every ANSI sequence.
F546   86 1B        CSI:      LDA   #27   
F548   8D 02                  BSR   gputc   
F54A   86 5B                  LDA   #"["   
F54C                          ENDIF      
F54C   7E FF 03     GPUTC:    JMP   CONOUT   
F54F                          IF   ANSI   
F54F                             ; `@ ( row col -- ): ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H. (ANSI counts from 1.)
F54F   8D F5        G_AT:     BSR   csi   
F551   BD F2 BE               JSR   h_swap   ; the row on top
F554   8D 0A                  BSR   pinc   
F556   86 3B                  LDA   #";"   
F558   8D F2                  BSR   gputc   
F55A   8D 04                  BSR   pinc   
F55C   86 48                  LDA   #"H"   
F55E   20 EC                  BRA   gputc   
F560                             ; pinc: print the top cell plus 1, unsigned, and drop it
F560   6C 41        PINC:     INC   1,U   
F562   26 02                  BNE   pi1   
F564   6C C4                  INC   ,U   
F566   7E F3 D0     PI1:      JMP   pdec   
F569                          ENDIF      
F569                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's own routines do the work (see the equates).
                    G_CLS:    JMP   CONCLS   
                    G_EOL:    JMP   CONEOL   
                    G_CUR:    LDD   ,U++   ; D = the flag, and the Z flag says the same
                              JMP   CONCUR   
                    G_AT:     LDD   ,U++   ; D = the column
                              LDX   ,U++   ; X = the row
                              JMP   CONAT   
F569                          ENDIF      
F569                          IF   CHECKED   
F569                          ;*Macro unroll:  LINERD                  ; the line reader of -n?
F569   8C FF 81     LINE:     CMPX   #-127   ; the line reader of -n?
F56C   24 04                  BHS   ln1   
F56E   86 81                  LDA   #-127   
F570   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F572   60 41        LN1:      NEG   1,U   
F574   8E 82 80               LDX   #LINEBUF   
F577   5F                     CLRB      
F578   BD F0 ED     LN2:      JSR   getk   
F57B   27 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
F57D   81 0D                  CMPA   #13   
F57F   27 16                  BEQ   ln5   
F581   81 08                  CMPA   #8   
F583   27 0C                  BEQ   ln4   
F585   E1 41                  CMPB   1,U   
F587   24 EF                  BHS   ln2   
F589   A7 85                  STA   B,X   
F58B   5C                     INCB      
F58C   BD FF 03     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
F58F   20 E7                  BRA   ln2   
F591   5D           LN4:      TSTB      
F592   27 E4                  BEQ   ln2   
F594   5A                     DECB      
F595   20 F5                  BRA   ln3   
F597   A7 85        LN5:      STA   B,X   
F599   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F59B   39                     RTS      
F59C                          ENDIF      
F59C                IMGEND:      


